From: Panurus maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 7/10] toolbox: one challenge domain per exact-l2 equation

___schwartz_zippel_accumulate_l2 combined the Z exact-l2 equations with the
same Schwartz-Zippel domain, so the verifier only checked their sum,
sum_i (||x_i||^2 + <pow2, upsilon_i> - B_i^2) = 0, and a prover could move
norm from one block to another through the upsilon slack
(lazer-crypto/lazer#25). Equation i now uses dom + i. With lambda >= 2 the
Z domains stay below the z4 domain lambda * (2 * (d - 1) + 2 + Z).

Applied to the toolbox copy in src/lin-proofs.c, which the lin_* proofs
run. It changes the transcript; proof sizes do not change.

Panurus-local patch, applied by `make lazer-install` (lazer.mk).

diff --git a/src/lin-proofs.c b/src/lin-proofs.c
index 4bdddbf..636b1e8 100644
--- a/src/lin-proofs.c
+++ b/src/lin-proofs.c
@@ -2895,9 +2895,16 @@ ___schwartz_zippel_accumulate_l2 (
       r1tptr[0] = r1t;
       r0tptr[0] = r0t;
 
+      /*
+       * one challenge domain per equation: with the same domain for all,
+       * only the sum of the Z exact-l2 equations was checked, and norm could
+       * be moved from one block to another (panurus patch,
+       * lazer-crypto/lazer#25). dom + i, i < Z, stays below the z4 domain
+       * lambda * (2 * (d - 1) + 2 + Z) since lambda >= 2.
+       */
       ___schwartz_zippel_accumulate2 (
           R2i, r1i, r0i, R2i2, r1i2, r0i2, R2tptr, r1tptr, r0tptr, 1, seed,
-          dom, params->quad_eval, u0, u1, u2, t0, t1, t2);
+          dom + i, params->quad_eval, u0, u1, u2, t0, t1, t2);
     }
 
   polyvec_free (tmp_polyvec);
